  "contracts": {
    "lem-emg-fieldstrength-positive-symmetric-reduction": {
      "citations": [
        {
          "fact": "F1",
          "source": "def-emg-lorentzian-forms",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "Write $\\mathrm{vol}_g$ for the oriented metric volume form of [[def-gr-metric-volume-form-and-current-flux]]; in any positively oriented chart it has components $\\sqrt{|\\det(g_{ab})|}\\,dx^0\\wedge dx^1\\wedge dx^2\\wedge dx^3$.",
          "uses": [
            "1.1",
            "2.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F2",
          "source": "lem-emg-observer-field-decomposition",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Equivalently, in any positively oriented future tetrad with $E_0=n$, and with $\\epsilon_{123}=+1$ in its oriented spatial triad, the components satisfy $F_{0i}=-E_i/c$ and $F_{ij}=\\epsilon_{ijk}B_k$.",
          "uses": [
            "1.1",
            "2.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F2",
          "source": "lem-emg-lorentz-hodge-calculus",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $(M,g,N,o)$ have the oriented, time-oriented Lorentzian structure and volume form of [[def-emg-lorentzian-forms]].",
          "uses": [
            "1.1",
            "2.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "L1",
          "source": "def-emg-electrovacuum-cauchy-system",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "Let $(M,g,N,o)$ be a smooth, Hausdorff, second-countable, oriented and time-oriented four-manifold with smooth Lorentz metric of signature $(-,+,+,+)$, as in [[def-emg-lorentzian-forms]].",
          "uses": [
            "1.1",
            "2.1",
            "4.1"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "derivations": [
        {
          "id": "step-1-1",
          "step": "1.1",
          "claim": "On a sufficiently small neighborhood the positive spatial metric makes each Gram–Schmidt denominator strictly positive. Hence the adapted orthonormal frame and its inverse coframe are smooth functions of $g$; differentiating the frame introduces only $g$ and $\\partial g$. In that frame the six components of $dF$ and $d\\star_gF$ with one normal slot are exactly the six evolution equations, while their all-spatial components are the two divergence constraints.",
          "inputs": [
            "given",
            "F1",
            "F2",
            "L1",
            "algebra"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "step-2-1",
          "step": "2.1",
          "claim": "Freeze the tetrad at a point and use its timelike vector as the time direction. The $(0,i,j)$ components of $dF=0$, with $F_{0i}=-e_i$ and $F_{ij}=\\epsilon_{ijk}b_k$, give $n(b)+\\operatorname{curl}e=0$. The spatial components of $\\nabla_aF^{ai}=0$, equivalent to $d\\star_gF=0$, give $n(e)-\\operatorname{curl}b=0$. Hence the spatial symbol in the convention $n(U)+A^j\\mathsf e_j(U)=0$ is $S(\\xi)$. Since $C(\\xi)^T=-C(\\xi)$, its two off-diagonal blocks are transposes and $S(\\xi)^T=S(\\xi)$. Also $|C(\\xi)v|^2=|\\xi|^2|v|^2-(\\xi\\cdot v)^2$, so $\\|C(\\xi)\\|=|\\xi|$ and $\\|S(\\xi)\\|=|\\xi|$.",
          "inputs": [
            "step 1.1",
            "F1",
            "F2",
            "L1",
            "algebra"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "step-3-1",
          "step": "3.1",
          "claim": "The identity $C(\\xi)^2v=\\xi(\\xi\\cdot v)-|\\xi|^2v$ shows that $-C(\\xi)^2$ has eigenvalues $0,|\\xi|^2,|\\xi|^2$. Squaring $S(\\xi)$ therefore gives eigenvalues $0,0,|\\xi|^2,|\\xi|^2,|\\xi|^2,|\\xi|^2$; because $S$ is symmetric and has trace zero, its eigenvalues are $0,0,|\\xi|,|\\xi|,-|\\xi|,-|\\xi|$. For any $z\\in\\mathbb R^6$, $z^TP(\\zeta)z\\ge(\\zeta(n)-|\\zeta_\\perp|_h)|z|^2$, proving positivity on the stated future covector cone. Taking $\\zeta=ds$ gives $ds(n)=\\alpha^{-1}$ and $\\zeta_\\perp=0$, hence the positive time matrix $\\alpha^{-1}I_6$. The shift contributes only scalar multiples of $I_6$ to spatial matrices, so those matrices remain symmetric.",
          "inputs": [
            "step 2.1",
            "algebra"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "step-4-1",
          "step": "4.1",
          "claim": "The frame-derivative, Hodge-coefficient, and commutator terms contain at most first derivatives of $g$ and no derivatives of $(e,b)$; they are smooth on the open state set where $g$ is Lorentzian, $\\alpha>0$, and $h>0$. This proves the claimed lower-order form and completes the conditional reduction proof.",
          "inputs": [
            "step 1.1",
            "step 3.1",
            "given",
            "L1",
            "algebra"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "routine_steps": [],
