          "evidence": "Statement clause4 and proof step 1.3 explicitly retain the coincident-endpoint time separation zero and its degenerate maximizer, rather than treating it as a positive-length causal curve."
        },
        {
          "case": "one",
          "status": "checked",
          "evidence": "Statement clause2 includes singleton compact sets K1={p},K2={q}; proof step 1.2 then gives the ordinary compact causal diamond, using the same compact-hull supplier."
        },
        {
          "case": "degenerate",
          "status": "checked",
          "evidence": "Proof step 1.3 keeps the r=q zero-length case;2.1 invokes coincident endpoints and imprisonment alternatives only at the limit-curve suppliers explicit hypotheses. No timelike equality characterization is extended to a returning or null-degenerate curve."
        },
        {
          "case": "endpoints",
          "status": "checked",
          "evidence": "Proof step 2.1 distinguishes bounded-length curves with both endpoint limits from the unbounded-length case yielding inextendible limit curves; Statement clause3 retains exactly those supplier endpoint hypotheses."
        },
        {
          "case": "nonempty-choice",
